# Vendored third-party code

## `basis_transcoder.js` + `basis_transcoder.wasm`

- Source: three.js r162 — `examples/jsm/libs/basis/`
  (https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/tree/r162/examples/jsm/libs/basis)
- Provenance: precompiled Emscripten build of the Basis Universal transcoder,
  shipped by the three.js project for its BasisTextureLoader/KTX2Loader.
- `basis_transcoder.js`: © the three.js authors, MIT License
  (https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/blob/r162/LICENSE).
- `basis_transcoder.wasm`: compiled from Basis Universal
  (https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal), © Binomial LLC,
  Apache License 2.0
  (https://github.com/BinomialLLC/basis_universal/blob/master/LICENSE).

Vendored verbatim (unmodified).  The wasm exposes the embind `BasisFile` /
`initializeBasis` API used by `classic-gfx/src/basis_web.rs` to transcode
`.basis` (ETC1S) payloads to the GPU's native compressed format on WebGL 2.

The transcoder is instantiated synchronously on the main thread (see
`transcoder/bootstrap.js`) via the Emscripten `instantiateWasm` hook, so the
synchronous `Gfx::add_texture_basis` load path can call it without an async
refactor.
